  "response_text": "If you receive an unexpected medical bill that you cannot cover with negotiation tips for creditors, here are some steps you can take:\n\n  1. Review the bill: Carefully review the bill to ensure that it is accurate and that all charges are correct. If you find any errors, contact the billing department to dispute the charges.\n  2. Contact the billing department: If you cannot resolve the issue with the billing department, contact the billing department to explain the situation and ask for assistance in resolving the issue.\n  3. Request a payment plan: If the bill is too large to pay in full at once, request a payment plan that allows you to pay the bill over time.\n  4. Consider filing for bankruptcy: If you cannot pay the bill and the bill is too large to pay in full, consider filing for bankruptcy. This will allow you to discharge the debt and avoid the costs of collection.\n  5. Seek help from a credit counseling agency: A credit counseling agency can help you develop a plan to pay off your debt and avoid the costs of collection.\n  6. Contact the billing department: If you are still unable to resolve the issue, contact the billing department to explain the situation and ask for assistance in resolving the issue.\n\nIt is important to take action as soon as possible to avoid additional fees and penalties.",
